Residual risk / notes
---------------------
- A 1 MiB adversarial flat-YAML is still ~tens of seconds under this cap; the cap
  bounds the WORST case, it does not make a 1 MiB pathological decode fast. To
  bound decode TIME rather than SIZE, a context-deadline around ReadInConfig (or
  the upstream O(1) fix) would be needed. The size cap is chosen because it
  mirrors the existing implicit cap and is a one-line, allocation-free stat.
- Operators with a legitimately huge --config (none known for dsd) would need the
  cap raised; it is a const, trivially tunable.
- Verified in a scratch copy (see verify/ in this directory): with the patch,
  a 2 MiB --config is rejected with the typed error and Load returns defaults;
  without it, Load decodes the file (slowly). Not applied to production.
